# The shared 10-layer chip stack: M2/M3 LOW plus eight TOP layers M4-M11, each
# pair coarser than the one below it, as real top metal is.
#
# SYMMETRIC UNITS, 10 SIGNAL TRACKS PER PERIOD.
#
# Every repeating unit is a PALINDROME: each rail carries the same gap before
# it as after it, so the pattern is invariant under reflection and a flipped
# instance's routing can land on real tracks.  (The gaps used to be lopsided —
# M2/M4 had 1 after a rail and 0.5 before — which left the H layers with NO
# reflection axis at any origin; see flow/chip/ReadMe.md.  Symmetry alone does
# not align a mirrored design: the ORIGIN has to put an axis on the instance
# centrelines, which is what chip_tracks_mirror.buda adds on top of this.)
#
# Each group carries FIVE signals rather than four — 10 per period instead of
# 8 — with the rail widths held and the signal width/spacing shrunk to fit.
# The PERIOD of every layer is unchanged, so the 504 = LCM(18,18,24,56)
# placement grid, `align_bottom_up` and every checked-in floorplan still hold;
# the bit pitch is period/10, a uniform 20% finer than the old period/8.
#
# EVERY VALUE IS BINARY-EXACT (a multiple of 1/16), and that is a HARD
# REQUIREMENT, not cosmetics.  `tracks_in_range` walks a period at a time with
# `pos += width + space_after`, so hundreds of periods of accumulated rounding
# decide whether a track sitting exactly ON a window edge is inside it.  The
# first cut of this stack used the arithmetically obvious 0.8 / 0.4 / 0.7 …
# (signal width and spacing scaled by exactly 8/10, which holds the signal
# metal per period EXACTLY constant) — and not one of those values is
# representable in binary.  The result was an off-by-one track at window edges
# that broke template alignment: check_template_tracks reported "397 vs 396",
# both cells went MISALIGNED, and the mirrored stack copied ZERO bits.
#
# Exact density and binary-exactness are mutually exclusive here: holding the
# metal needs w = 0.8*w_old, which is never a binary fraction.  Exactness wins,
# so the density moves slightly and the def_layer overheads below move with it
# (the widest miss is M2-M5, 55.56% -> 58.33%).  Widths keep each layer's
# original width:spacing ratio.
#
#   layer  period  rail    w       s       g      overhead (was)   bit pitch (was)
#   M2-M5    18     2     0.75   0.375   0.875    58.33 (55.56)    1.80  (2.25)
#   M6       24     3     0.75   0.75    1.125    68.75 (66.67)    2.40  (3.00)
#   M7       39     6     1.625  0.8125  1.0625   58.33 (58.97)    3.90  (4.875)
#   M8/M9    56     8     2.375  1.1875  1.6875   57.59 (57.14)    5.60  (7.00)
#   M10/M11  74    10     3.25   1.625   2.125    56.08 (56.76)    7.40  (9.25)
#
# Overhead percentages are the patterns' measured values (1 - signal density) —
# see report_overhead below.
def_layer  2 M2  H LOW 58.33
def_layer  3 M3  V LOW 58.33
def_layer  4 M4  H TOP 58.33
def_layer  5 M5  V TOP 58.33
def_layer  6 M6  H TOP 68.75
def_layer  7 M7  V TOP 58.33
def_layer  8 M8  H TOP 57.59
def_layer  9 M9  V TOP 57.59
def_layer 10 M10 H TOP 56.08
def_layer 11 M11 V TOP 56.08

# Track patterns are REQUIRED for Detailed NUTS.
# Format: <layer_id> <origin> [<type> <width> <spacing>] ...
def_track_pattern 2  -100   POWER 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875  GROUND 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875
def_track_pattern 3  0      POWER 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875  GROUND 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875
def_track_pattern 4  -200   POWER 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875  GROUND 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875
def_track_pattern 5  0      POWER 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875  GROUND 2 0.875  SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.375 SIGNAL 0.75 0.875
def_track_pattern 6  -400   POWER 3 1.125  SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 1.125  GROUND 3 1.125  SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 0.75 SIGNAL 0.75 1.125
def_track_pattern 7  -600   POWER 6 1.0625  SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 1.0625  GROUND 6 1.0625  SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 0.8125 SIGNAL 1.625 1.0625
def_track_pattern 8  -800   POWER 8 1.6875  SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.6875  GROUND 8 1.6875  SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.6875
def_track_pattern 9  -1000  POWER 8 1.6875  SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.6875  GROUND 8 1.6875  SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.1875 SIGNAL 2.375 1.6875
def_track_pattern 10 -1200  POWER 10 2.125  SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 2.125  GROUND 10 2.125  SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 2.125
def_track_pattern 11 -1400  POWER 10 2.125  SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 2.125  GROUND 10 2.125  SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 1.625 SIGNAL 3.25 2.125

report_overhead
